id: core/projection-and-aperture
title: "Projection, View, lens, and aperture"
kind: interface-boundary-contract
status: draft-0.5
updated: 2026-09-05

definitions:
  projection: "what an attributed Agent actually expresses, represents, proposes, commits, or attempts into an Arena"
  view: "a purpose-specific rebuildable rendering over canonical IDs and events"
  lens: "a named View rule that foregrounds particular relations"
  aperture: "the scope, depth, time window, and salience included in a view"
  aperture_preset: "a named user-facing binding of a versioned View, aperture parameters, presentation profile, temporal cursor, and fallback; the interface may label this simply Aperture"
  effective_projection: "canonical state at an event cursor intersected with viewer/source grants, then filtered by the selected View and aperture and rendered through the effective presentation profile"
  orientation_map: "a time-indexed rebuildable View of attributed orientation coverage; never a second canonical state store"
  orientation_inquiry: "a question-facing View that renders one orientation_map lacuna without changing semantic state"
  perspective_field: "a question-, claim-, expression-, relationship-, or move-facing View of attributed standpoints, answer candidates, evidence relations, disagreement, and feedback; never a vote tally or second belief store"
  presentation_profile: "scoped and revisable View preferences for wording, order, pacing, density, medium, interaction, and accessibility; never a fixed learning-style diagnosis"
  publication: "an authorized versioned public or shared projection; never a duplicate truth store or grant to underlying private state"

known_views:
  - arena
  - timeline
  - proof-and-replay
  - memory
  - causal-graph
  - filesystem
  - world
  - orientation_map
  - orientation_inquiry
  - perspective_field
  - yawn_temporal_header
  - ranked_move_deliberation
  - yawnbot_agentic_embodiment

orientation_presentation_boundary:
  semantic_source: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  selection_policy: core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  accepted_preference_contract: schemas/projection-preference.v1.schema.json
  aperture_registry_contract: interface/aperture-registry-and-provisioning-v0.1.yawn
  perspective_field_contract: interface/perspective-field-and-feedback-reintegration-v0.1.yawn
  rule: >
    question_key, answer-candidate identity, source, and meaning survive a change
    of wording, order, layout, representation medium, answer input adapter, or
    registered aperture. Inferred presentation fit remains a proposal until
    accepted; measured usefulness is a separate scoped claim.

runtime_boundary:
  equation: >
    effective projection = canonical semantic state at event cursor INTERSECT
    effective viewer/source grants FILTERED by registered View and aperture
    parameters RENDERED through the effective presentation profile.
  user_control: >
    A user may select Auto, choose a permitted registered aperture, temporarily
    override it, or save an accepted preference at a declared scope. Aperture
    selection and provisioning remain separate controls.
  default_rule: >
    Questions First is a strong context default for sparse private Yawns;
    Attention Frontier may lead at a longitudinal root; anonymous viewers receive
    only an explicitly published public projection. These are policy defaults,
    not a closed global enum.

invariants:
  - "Timeline is a view, not a Yawn kind."
  - "Agent Arena is a View, not canonical state."
  - "Perspective Field is a View over attributed answers, voices, evidence, and feedback, not a vote tally or canonical belief store."
  - "A voice is an expression from a standpoint; it is not automatically an Agent, Yawnbot, psychological part, belief, or truth."
  - "Question priority, answer credence, perspective relevance, popularity, conviction, salience, and move leverage remain distinguishable."
  - "Renderer, layout, color, image, and navigation state are View concerns unless an Agent expresses them into an Arena."
  - "An Agent Projection remains distinct from its Intention, another Agent's Observation, and the resulting Consequence."
  - "Aperture changes visibility and salience, not truth or permission."
  - "An aperture may only narrow or reorganize data already available through effective grants."
  - "Selecting an aperture never changes sharing, provisioning, semantic state, or effect authority."
  - "Changing provisioning never silently changes the user's selected aperture."
  - "Public and private projections are not separate canonical truth stores."
  - "A public View exposes only explicitly provisioned fields and source-safe derivatives."
  - "Aperture availability is registry-driven and permission-filtered, not a hard-coded UI union."
  - "Every interactive rendered object resolves to a stable canonical ID."
  - "Presentation-only events do not alter semantic state."
  - "Color and spatial position never carry semantics alone."
  - "Presentation preference is not a learning-style diagnosis or semantic claim."
  - "A View preference cannot hide safety, authority, privacy, provenance, semantic coverage, disagreement, or proof."
  - "Selecting a historical replay moment changes temporal aperture, not canonical state."
  - "Historical replay can never widen current access rights."
  - "Opening an advocate/challenger deliberation changes explanatory aperture, not rank, choice, authority, or proof."
  - "A forecast trace is attributed model history, not a market price or world fact."
  - "Public feedback is an attributed input; popularity, praise, criticism, or engagement cannot directly become truth, reward, policy, authority, or proof."
  - "Giving a Yawn an agentic character or bot body changes embodiment and interaction, not semantic identity, consciousness, truth, authority, or proof."
  - "A Yawnbot embodiment resolves to explicit Yawn, Agent, intelligence, capability, authority, and provisioning references rather than collapsing them into one character."
  - "Custom or executable apertures cannot bypass source, field, identity, privacy, consent, authority, or proof gates."

